.TH grokbot-tui-mcp-serve 1  "serve " 
.SH NAME
grokbot\-tui\-mcp\-serve \- Run the MCP server (stdio by default; \-\-http for streamable HTTP on localhost)
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBgrokbot\-tui mcp serve\fR [\fB\-\-stdio\fR] [\fB\-\-http\fR] [\fB\-\-read\-only\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Run the MCP server (stdio by default; \-\-http for streamable HTTP on localhost)
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-stdio\fR
Serve over stdin/stdout (default)
.TP
\fB\-\-http\fR [\fI<ADDR>\fR]
Serve streamable HTTP at ADDR (loopback only; default from mcp.toml, else 127.0.0.1:8765). Clients send `Authorization: Bearer <grokbot\-tui mcp token>`
.TP
\fB\-\-read\-only\fR
Refuse send_message and answer_card for this run (overrides mcp.toml)
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
